WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.100
There are various strategies employed by space pirates.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.440
Some involve frontal assaults, guns blazing,

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.440
some involve waiting in ambush,

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.360
and some use boarding parties
and man-to-man combat.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.360
But regardless which is used,

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.160
bringing the enemy ship's systems
under your control is critical.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.790
Electronic warfare is a quiet battle,

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.290
fought without guns or hand-to-hand combat.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.120
The losing ship cedes control

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:29.550
of its life support systems to the enemy.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.300
Don't blame me for what happens.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:35.010
Make the best decision you can.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:13.440
Ahem!

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:14.940
What?

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:17.450
We need something to get started.

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:18.950
What kind of something?

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:20.740
"Begin the operation!"

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.700
Or something like that.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.080
Electronic warfare isn't a gunfight.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:27.580
You wait quietly,
leaving the enemy alone,

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.460
and then, keeping your guard up, you sneak in.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:33.590
It probably isn't what you think it is.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:37.010
Well, you've never done it either, right, Chiaki?

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.630
Chiaki?

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:39.680
All right!

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:42.850
I'm booting up the Odette II's
electronic warfare system.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:47.100
If we get totally outmatched,
we pull the plug.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.730
Won't that break it?

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:53.110
You can't engage in electronic warfare
if you're that hesitant.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:54.190
Listen...

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:56.320
No way!

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.820
It's begun communicating on its own!

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.030
What?

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.030
Wait, where is it connecting to?

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:06.540
It's connecting to a database somewhere.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.120
Um...

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.960
The Stellar Military's Records Division?

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:21.630
Automatic defenses?

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.050
Could this be...

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.510
I knew it.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:29.890
These are one-way communications
to the D-block docking port.

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:31.350
What does that mean?

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:33.270
When the electronic warfare system booted up,

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:36.150
it started fighting the enemy, I think...

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:45.030
U-Um, what's this?

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.120
Oh, no!

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:53.540
All on-board power is being routed
to the electronic warfare system.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:56.000
It's drawing four times as much
power from outside...

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:56.750
Five times?

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.430
Wow!

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:04.840
It's retaking the system!

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:06.180
Keep going!  Keep going!

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:07.510
How about you help me?!
Keep going!

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:08.560
How about you help me?!

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:15.560
Huh?

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.860
The dock-side breaker tripped.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:21.490
This system has a bigger appetite
than we anticipated.

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:23.320
We almost won too.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.540
It's safely reactivated.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:32.000
Is power also back on inside the ship?

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.660
Probably.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.880
Next time, we'll need to have them

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:37.590
increase the power to this ship.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:38.880
Before that...

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:45.930
You're in charge of our excuse.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:49.390
I wonder what we should say...

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:02.860
She accidentally pressed the switch, huh?

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:04.110
Yup.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:08.830
And what of the attacking cargo ship?

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.620
They panicked and ran.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:13.790
Don't know where to.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.750
Smart move.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.250
The practice cruise is still ahead.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.920
This time, they were probably just looking.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:26.340
Not that it matters,
but you're pretty relaxed today.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:28.390
Is the yacht club okay?

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:31.560
The upperclassmen are drawing up
the Odette II's flight plan.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:34.020
The lowerclassmen are working on
the yacht simulator.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:37.940
It's better if they learn to stand on
their own, rather than having

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:40.400
a new advisor show them everything.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.570
Stand on their own, huh?

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:45.440
Finals are coming up,

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.530
so we should give them some room.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.240
Right, right.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:58.370
Okay!

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.750
I'm leaving early!

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:13.560
Here you go.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:20.230
Your fans haven't come back.

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:21.730
Do you want them to?

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:23.610
So you could call them, huh?

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:25.740
I said...

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:28.780
Chiaki!

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:32.240
Don't give me that.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:40.250
A non-aggression pact.

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.170
A non-aggression pact?

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:45.960
Interfering with Kato Marika

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:48.670
is forbidden in New Okuhama City.

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:51.140
However, this only extends until

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:53.010
the Letter of Marque's renewal date.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:54.970
What happens after that is up for debate.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:57.520
What does that mean?

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.650
After you become an official pirate,

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:04.480
they'll include you in their discussions
as to what happens next.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:08.570
But I haven't said I would yet.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:10.030
What are you talking about?

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:11.070
Huh?

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:13.320
I said, "What are you talking about?"
to the girl who was

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:15.450
thrilled at the prospect
of electronic warfare.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:16.490
Thrilled?

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:17.910
Really?

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:19.210
Don't run from it, okay?

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:22.290
Your teacher is a pirate.

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.340
Shady people pursue you.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:28.090
This practice cruise will be full of danger.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:30.510
And there's a mysterious transfer student!

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:32.220
It'll be fine.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:34.430
It's a great chance to go into space.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.260
I'm going on the practice cruise.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:39.730
And I don't think they're all enemies.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.690
I hope not.

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:45.860
Exams, huh?

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:48.440
I guess we'll see how far
last-minute cramming goes.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:50.490
So what was Chiaki doing there?

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:51.650
Dunno.

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:53.490
Maybe she just likes our parfaits?

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:57.580
It looks like you have lots of problems.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.120
But you seem to be having fun.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:00.370
Really?

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:02.670
Sometimes, I wonder...

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:05.330
Is it really okay for me to be your friend?

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.500
You are my friend.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:10.630
You're more levelheaded
than any of my other friends.

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:14.090
I'm kind of an airhead, so having
you around really helps.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:16.890
You're going to float all the way
into space with all that air.

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:17.930
That's silly.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:23.770
Can I expect a present?

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.270
I'll consider it.

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:27.190
When you get back,
let's go to the sea, okay?

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:28.220
Yeah.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:43.000
So, when are they?

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.540
Huh?

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:46.380
Exams start tomorrow.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:48.090
They're in a hurry.

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:50.340
Isn't summer break pretty long?

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:53.260
I can mess around for the
rest of the summer.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:55.840
I've saved up plenty of cash.

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:59.100
Your job is fine,
but how about the other thing?

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.520
Well, you know...

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:04.190
Ririka.

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:08.310
The non-aggression pact...

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:11.280
What's that?

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:14.570
Oh, it's nothing.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:34.470
Okay, close your textbooks.

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:35.800
Got it!

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.750
It's over...

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:16.220
All right, pass your answer sheets forward.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:18.430
Okay!

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:23.390
Excuse me!

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:25.770
My, don't you look like a teacher.

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:27.430
Don't make fun of me.

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:29.400
I've gotta make up a grade sheet.

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:32.110
I don't just look like a teacher...
I am one.

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:34.230
Then, here's a present.

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.320
What happened after that?

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.950
Is someone going after the Odette II?

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:43.200
Nope.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.910
They're probably waiting for
it to launch into space.

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:51.130
Tell the Bentenmaru to keep an eye out.

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:54.380
Here's to the students and
their hard-working teacher.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.140
Is everyone here?

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.350
Yeah!

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:13.270
Last up is our doctor.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:15.860
It's Ms. Misa!

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:20.950
Ms. Misa! Ms. Misa!

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:23.910
Everyone, it's finally time
for our practice cruise.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:28.040
Some of you will be going
into space for the first time.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:32.670
But I'm sure these few days
will be quite useful

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:34.750
in the rest of your lives.

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:37.300
Now, let's go!

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.010
Yeah!

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:51.690
This is the Odette II.

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:54.980
Hakuoh Academy Yacht Club
President, Jenny Dolittle.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:59.150
The Odette II will now depart
from docking bay C68.

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:02.150
This is Sea of the Morningstar Relay Station.

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:03.160
Roger that.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:15.710
Forward at minimum speed.

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:32.100
We have exited the control space of

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:34.140
the Sea of the Morningstar Relay Station.

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:36.730
Passing space speed 3.

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:40.110
Switching coordinate systems from
Sea of the Morningstar to Tau Ceti.

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:48.410
We're fine now.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:50.830
First, everyone, good work.

00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:59.590
As you can see,

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:02.260
our course will take us around Tau Ceti,

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:04.380
and back to the relay station.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:08.430
By passing close to the planet Sand of
the Red Star, orbiting across from us,

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:11.020
we'll absorb four hundred times the

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:13.930
thermal radiation that Sea of
the Morningstar gets.

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:15.980
But we'll be all right.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:19.940
As Odette II receives the sunlight,

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:22.070
its speed will approach maximum.

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:24.950
But still, this is a sailing ship.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:29.160
These days, it's rare to see
such a relaxed flight plan.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:32.660
A normal spaceship could make it
there and back within a day.

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:35.460
But the Odette II will be using

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:39.880
only two percent of the
approach energy in the process.

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:41.920
It's a nice bonus.

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.050
However, that means

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:47.340
we must constantly monitor the
ship and our surroundings.

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:50.260
This is the perfect club activity.

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:51.510
Now, let's all do our best.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:52.560
Right!

00:13:58.020 --> 00:14:02.110
The Odette II will now deploy its masts.

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:05.190
Please confirm that no ships
are in the surrounding area.

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:07.320
Radar has been checked.

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:08.990
Nothing on the transponder, either.

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:10.780
No problems for now.

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:12.160
Roger.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:13.120
Now, then...

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:14.370
Initiate mast deployment.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:19.080
Deploy the mizzen-mast,
the main-mast, and then the fore-mast.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:19.920
Roger.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:31.300
What happened?

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:33.560
What's going on?

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:35.100
Right!

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.520
The upper yard opened before

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:39.770
the main-mast was raised.

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:41.560
And now it's tangled.

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:43.980
You tried everything you
could to fix it, right?

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:44.780
Yes.

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:48.990
So the automatic systems can't fix this, huh?

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:52.990
What happens if we remove the safety
and force it up anyway?

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:57.960
In the worst case, we'd lose a third
of the upper twelve o'clock mast.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:02.380
Not only would propulsion drop,

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:06.800
but it's bad luck to damage
a ship right after launch.

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:10.930
Did we load any work pods on board?

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:12.300
No.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:14.560
And we have no worker robots, either.

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:15.680
You knew that, right?

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:18.850
I was just checking.

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:20.730
Well, freshmen...

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:22.860
It's time for a spacewalk.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:28.820
I'm surprised.

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:31.860
So this is how modern spacesuits look, huh?

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:34.410
Even the safety checks are fully automatic.

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:37.120
This is Kane.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:38.950
Bridge, can you hear me?

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:40.040
Loud and clear.

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:41.330
We have video too.

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:43.880
Leave your communication channel open.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:48.300
Unless I give specific orders otherwise,
we'll all use the same line.

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:51.180
And unless there are special circumstances,

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:54.930
use the same line for
communications from the bridge.

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:57.010
What would constitute a
special circumstance?

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:00.600
An emergency that you couldn't let the

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:02.850
students outside the ship know about.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:04.730
Or perhaps if we didn't want to let

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:08.030
anyone know people were outside the ship.

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.570
I'll leave the decision to you.

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:13.740
An emergency, huh?

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:23.670
No!  Lilly, you pervert!

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:25.960
Come on, give up!

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:27.420
Hey, don't do that!

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:28.840
Wait!  Stop!

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:37.180
I have to take a half dozen
of these outside?

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:39.310
I can hear you, Advisor.

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:45.400
This was...

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:49.940
his idea.

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:54.610
Are our suits all right?

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:57.450
Put on your helmets, and let's
make sure they're airtight.

00:16:58.030 --> 00:17:02.120
If there's a problem,
the suit should tell you.

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:04.290
Once your helmet's on,

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.420
you won't be able to hear anything external.

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.960
Don't forget to turn on your
communication systems.

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:12.760
And once you're out there,
even if hair gets in your eyes,

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:14.680
you won't be able to fix it.

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:17.680
So make sure your hair is pulled back.

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:22.600
Prep room to bridge.

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:25.390
Are all communication channels open?

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:29.020
We're receiving data from seven,
including yours.

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:34.280
We've started receiving and recording
the monitoring camera and bio-data.

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:36.660
All of you are one unit now.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:39.530
Everything you see,
as well as your vital readings,

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:41.540
will be part of the ship's log.

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:43.290
Seriously?

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:45.370
It's only for a few hours.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:46.870
Put up with it.

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:50.840
Then, close your face shields.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:52.500
Once we've verified they're airtight,

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:54.130
let's open the door and exit.

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:56.130
Standby

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:09.980
Depressurizing

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:12.270
Is anyone not feeling well?

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:22.240
I'm opening the extra-vehicular workroom.

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:37.260
Let's go outside.

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:38.620
Follow me.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:41.140
The outside...

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:04.910
Okay, listen up!

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:07.660
Don't be surprised by what you see now.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:20.010
This is amazing.

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:22.050
Let's go, everyone.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:34.650
I figured that mast was going
to get stuck on something...

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:36.530
Kane to bridge.

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:37.480
Can you see it?

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:38.650
We can.

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:41.320
Can you tell where it's stuck?

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:42.740
As we thought,

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:47.410
one of the yards that wasn't supposed
to extend did, and got caught.

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:48.910
Something like that.

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:49.830
Advisor!

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:51.580
Do you see that?

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:54.580
Yeah, I see.

00:19:57.500 --> 00:19:59.550
What do you think, Marika?

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:00.670
Well,

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:02.510
if we change the bracing angle

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:05.260
on the yard that's stuck...

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:08.560
We could slip it past, before deploying it.

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:10.680
What do you think, bridge?

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:14.650
In this phase, the yards aren't fixed.

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:16.520
If you don't really force it...

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:17.520
That should work!

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:18.820
That's right.

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:20.490
We'll lose less time than if we

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:23.820
fully retract and then raise the mast again.

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:26.370
Let's follow Marika's plan.

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:27.870
Roger.

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:30.540
Everyone, follow her orders.

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:34.420
Whenever you move anything,
make sure to say so.

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:35.710
Roger.

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:39.420
Marika, you'll give the
order to raise the mast.

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:41.670
Everything will begin on your word.

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:42.510
Yes, sir!

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:46.220
The positions of all seven have been confirmed.

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:56.480
We also have a good read on the pressure
everyone is exerting on the mast.

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:58.770
Marika, you may begin.

00:20:58.770 --> 00:20:59.730
Roger.

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:01.570
Marika to bridge.

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:03.950
Please try to raise the mast again.

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:05.990
Raising main-mast.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:15.710
Main-mast deploying.

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:16.960
All areas green.

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.250
No problems.

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:23.300
This is the bridge.

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:25.550
Raising mast to normal position.

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:27.050
Understood.

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:31.470
We'll do a full inspection, then return inside.

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:32.600
Roger.

00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:43.530
Are you looking out into space?

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:46.490
Sea of the Morningstar is pretty.

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:50.030
But it's so small.

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:54.290
Everyone's just a dot in space, aren't they?

00:21:54.660 --> 00:21:56.040
Are you scared?

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:57.120
Yes.

00:21:58.580 --> 00:22:02.000
However, I'm looking forward to it.

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:08.260
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:11.470
The Odette II Leaves Port
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:12.470
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:12.470 --> 00:22:17.980
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:17.980 --> 00:22:20.980
Welcome glory, let's breakthrough and fly out now, let's go!

00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:24.360
Run towards an unlimited dimension. Come, let's accelerate beyond this

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:27.450
history that's to be known, regardless of time. Fly towards a destined future.

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:30.490
Just a fossil if you give up a miracle. Your decision is your best choice.

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:39.420
There's another, unknown, me hiding in my heart.

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:44.300
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:48.130
How far?

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:50.800
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell! Go, go, ring, ring a bell!

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:54.430
Until the end.

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:55.770
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell!

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:59.100
You're lost and missing.

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:07.940
We're lost without a hope of any shelter.

00:23:07.940 --> 00:23:11.700
But why? What did we do? What did we do?

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:13.120
What should we do?

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:16.290
From the world beyond shadows invade.

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:20.580
We're destined to stop them with our lives.

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:26.630
So no matter where we go, as far as it takes

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:30.880
we'll always believe in ourselves.

00:23:40.730 --> 00:23:43.270
A mysterious shadow follows
the fun practice cruise.

00:23:44.190 --> 00:23:46.320
What is the best choice she's made,

00:23:46.320 --> 00:23:48.400
not as potential captain of a pirate ship,

00:23:48.400 --> 00:23:50.700
but as a normal high school girl,

00:23:50.700 --> 00:23:52.160
as a member of the yacht club?

00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:55.660
Next time, on <i>Bodacious Space Pirates:</i>

00:23:55.660 --> 00:23:57.290
The final battle is at midnight.

00:23:57.290 --> 00:23:58.950
Look forward to it.

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:04.960
The Final Battle is at Midnight

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:10.220
Everyone's just a dot in space.
